(6. Business Rules) Tj
T*
(=================) Tj
T*
( - Invoice statuses are DRAFT, DUE, PARTIALLY_PAID, PAID, OVERDUE, and CANCELLED.) Tj
T*
( - Draft save creates no voucher; final create/finalize posts vouchers automatically.) Tj
T*
( - Initial paid amount creates Receipt voucher; remaining due creates Journal voucher.) Tj
T*
( - Later due collection creates Receipt voucher and a payment history row.) Tj
T*
( - Refund creates Payment voucher and a refund history row; reports include refund totals.) Tj
T*
( - Full paid invoices have disabled Edit Invoice button in view page for design consistency.) Tj
T*
( - Delete is restricted to Draft or Cancelled invoices to protect audit/report history.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Data Requirements) Tj
T*
(====================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Entity | Main Fields | Notes) Tj
T*
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Invoice | branchId, customerId, invoiceNo, invoiceDate, dueDate, status, totals, paidAmount,) Tj
T*
(dueAmount | Unique by branchId + invoiceNo; indexed by branch/status/date.) Tj
T*
(InvoiceItem | itemType, name, description, quantity, unitPrice, lineTotal | Quantity whole) Tj
T*
(number in UI/validation; relation cascades with invoice.) Tj
T*
(InvoicePayment | invoiceId, paymentAccountId, voucherId, amount, paymentDate, method,) Tj
T*
(referenceNo, note | Refund can be represented as method Refund or negative payment amount.) Tj
T*
(InvoiceVoucher | invoiceId, voucherId, postingType, amount | Posting types include) Tj
T*
(INITIAL_PAID, INITIAL_DUE, COLLECTION, REFUND, REVERSAL.) Tj
T*
(InvoiceAuditLog | invoiceId, branchId, userId, action, description, data | Maintains) Tj
T*
(operational traceability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Non-functional Requirements) Tj
T*
(==============================) Tj
T*
(- Security: JWT authentication, role permission, and branch permission checks must be) Tj
T*
(enforced on every API.) Tj
T*
(- Accuracy: monetary calculations must use decimal precision and avoid stale paid/due/status) Tj
T*
(values.) Tj
T*
(- Responsiveness: invoice pages must work on desktop, laptop, tablet, and very small mobile) Tj
T*
(views without clipped content.) Tj
T*
(- Auditability: finalized invoices must remain available for report history except allowed) Tj
T*
(Draft/Cancelled delete cases.) Tj
T*
(- Performance: list/report queries should use pagination, branch filtering, and indexed) Tj
T*
(status/date fields.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Acceptance Criteria) Tj
T*
(======================) Tj
T*
(- Users can create, save draft, finalize, edit, cancel, restore draft, delete allowed) Tj
T*
(invoices, collect due payment, edit payment, and refund within permission limits.) Tj
T*
(- Payment history shows each payment/refund with date, account, method, reference, voucher,) Tj
T*
(amount, and actions only where required.) Tj
T*
(- Summary report totals match invoice totals, paid amounts, refund amounts, due amounts, and) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
